From 9fd91d12616e19b5832c1f2d49de2a05bea5d667 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dario Gabriel Lipicar <dario@status.im>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:14:40 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] feat(sync): fetch matched blocks in the background

UpdateSubscriber::fetch_blocks_with takes a function that fetches a
matched block by other means than the node's peers (a Tor errand, in the
wallet core). Each block's fetch starts as its filter matches, while the
scan goes on, so a slow fetch never holds the filters back in the
unbounded event channel.

Fetched blocks are applied oldest first, up to the first still under
way. scanned() stays below that block, so a restart checks its filter
again, and synced() is false while any fetch is pending. At the tip,
each fetch that lets blocks apply makes an update. The fetcher answers
None for a block no longer in the chain, which is skipped. checked() is
the last filter checked, whether or not a fetch holds scanned() back.
